import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Positions"><PageHero title="Join the group" intro="We welcome researchers who are curious, collaborative, and motivated by open computational science."/><section class="section white"><div class="container"><article class="opportunity grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Graduate students</p><h2>Build a research path across disciplines.</h2></div><div class="prose"><h3>Prospective students</h3><p>Apply to the <a href="https://gradschool.princeton.edu/academics/degrees-requirements/fields-study">Princeton Graduate School</a> and specify your interest in the Rosen Group. Students from any department are welcome; the <a href="https://cbe.princeton.edu/graduate">Chemical and Biological Engineering Ph.D.</a> and <a href="https://materials.princeton.edu/phd">Materials Science and Engineering Ph.D.</a> programs are especially relevant.</p><h3>Admitted students</h3><p>If you have been offered admission or are already a Princeton student, email Prof. Rosen to learn about current opportunities.</p></div></article><article class="opportunity grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Postdoctoral researchers</p><h2>Bring an ambitious computational idea.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Exceptional candidates may email Prof. Rosen with the subject line “Postdoc Opportunity,” a CV, and a short description of research interests. Please note that Prof. Rosen is not able to respond to all inquiries.</p><p>Candidates are strongly encouraged to apply for university-sponsored fellowships when applicable. For applications requiring nomination, include the fellowship, a CV, and a few sentences about the research you hope to pursue.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://rosengroup.slite.page/p/Npb-mCkGnHndP1/Fellowships-and-Awards#5df5cbe1">Fellowship guide ↗</a></div></article><article class="opportunity grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Undergraduates</p><h2>Start doing research at Princeton.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Projects are regularly available for Princeton undergraduates, often for course credit through junior independent work or a senior thesis. Students from any department are welcome, though Python experience is generally expected.</p><p>Email Prof. Rosen with a résumé or CV and the areas that interest you.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:asrosen@princeton.edu">Email Prof. Rosen</a></div></article></div></section></BaseLayout><style>.opportunity{padding:4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.opportunity:first-child{padding-top:0}</style>
